# Environment files (secrets)
#
# ★ 2026-08-23 — WIDENED FROM `*.local` ONLY. The previous three lines let four real
# secrets files into the build context: `.env.blog` (7,896 bytes, carries the session
# cookie key, the email encryption key and the DB URL), `docker/.env`,
# `apps/blog/.env.testing` and `apps/blog/.env.mirrornet-testing`. `Dockerfile:20` is
# `COPY . .` into the BUILDER stage, and `docker-bake.hcl` exports builder layers to a
# registry cache with `mode=max` — so anything left here travels off-box even though the
# final runner image is clean.
#
# Verified before widening: NO stage reads an env file from the context. The builder takes
# build-time values from ARG/ENV, and the runner copies only the entrypoint, next.config.js,
# package.json, .next/standalone, .next/static, public and lib/markdowns. `react-env`
# supplies runtime values from the container environment at start, not from a context file.
#
# No `!*.example` negation: no stage needs the examples either, and a negation is one more
# thing to get wrong.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Build caches (rebuilt in Docker)
.turbo
**/.turbo
**/.next
**/node_modules
node_modules
**/dist
**/.cache

